cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the v0.2.0 manuscript."
title: "Legibility Is Not Deployability: Four Gates for LLM-Assisted Prediction-Market Trading"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Abel AI Lab"
    affiliation: "Abel AI Lab"
    email: lab@abel.ai
version: "v0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-05-06"
abstract: >-
  This repository packages the manuscript, data registries, the Evidence
  Locator, and minimal reproduction checks for Paper 2 from Abel AI Lab.
  The paper distills four operational gates—sourceability, fillability,
  capacity, and anchor stability—that repeatedly erased apparent
  LLM-accessible edges in retail prediction-market trading research, and
  formalizes ceiling-pin layer migration as a cross-mechanism failure
  mode. Scope is a single-lab, single-period failure-preserving corpus:
  13 active campaigns, 156 instrumented adversarial-review rounds, 225
  recovered route decisions, 52 strict attack rows, 40 quote-bank rows,
  and zero durable greater-than-$1k/month retail deployment routes.
keywords:
  - prediction-markets
  - LLM-trading
  - ceiling-pin
  - layer-migration
  - anchoring-bias
  - abelian-methodology
  - failure-preserving-corpus
  - preregistration
  - retrospective
